    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2VvsAv9bMnVw5hmscGggixs)_\n\n## What\nWith the plain posframe of #156 the `M-x` glitch is gone. This puts the minibuffer text size back, in a way that follows `text-scale-adjust`:\n\n- `sp-minibuffer` maps the fontaine face `sp-minibuffer-face` (1.36 of `default` in `regular`, the same as `sp-text-face` in Org) onto `default`, as before.\n- It then calls `text-scale-set` with the `text-scale-mode-amount` of the window that was selected when the minibuffer opened. So `s-=` / `s--` / `s-0` in a buffer scale the text of the next `M-x`, file picker or note picker in step with the buffer's text. A minibuffer that is already open does not change size.\n- It is on `minibuffer-setup-hook` (the selected window is only known there), not `minibuffer-mode-hook`.\n- It does not reset `face-remapping-alist`, which is what dropped the text scale in #146.\n\nDocs (`sp-fonts.org`) and CHANGELOG updated.\n\n## Reading of the request\nI read \"the size of the text equals the fontaine face\" as: the base size is the fontaine face (`sp-minibuffer-face`), not a size of its own. Org text still uses `sp-text-face` as before. If you wanted the minibuffer at the plain `default` size, change the first line of `sp-minibuffer`.\n\n## Not tested\nNothing was run in Emacs (none in the container). The glitch's cause was never found, and this text size was active while it happened (#146 to #154). If it returns, remove `(add-hook 'minibuffer-setup-hook #'sp-minibuffer)` first.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiBs9srTW9kUiGXduSF)_",
